# ── What is and is not committed under data/ ──────────────────────────────────
#
# Stage OUTPUTS are committed, so the app is clone-and-run with no API pull.
# Everything under data/raw/ is an INPUT and is ignored wholesale, because every
# one of them is re-fetchable by re-running its stage:
#
#   data/raw/cache/    the polite-fetch HTTP cache. Scratch by definition.
#   data/raw/media/    full-resolution federal renderings, ~34 MB. Stage 01
#                      derives the committed thumb/ and web/ variants from these.
#   data/raw/statcan/  bulk cube zips, ~28 MB. Stage 02 reads and discards them.
#   data/raw/geo/      Natural Earth + StatCan boundaries, ~129 MB. The committed
#                      artifacts are web/public/geo/, built by scripts/build_geo.mjs.
#
# The rule is deliberately the whole directory rather than a list. An earlier
# version listed only cache/ and media/, and 28 MB of cube zips were committed
# before anyone noticed — a per-directory allowlist fails open, which is the
# wrong direction for a rule about repository weight.
data/raw/
